<title>SPAIN: Spain Jan industrial production rose 2.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Spain Jan industrial production rose 2.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Statistics Institute gave the following provisional figures (percentage change):</p>
<p> INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION		  JAN 97    DEC 96  JAN 96</p>
<p> Yr/yr					 2.9	  1.8   -1.2</p>
<p> Avg yr to date against yr ago	 2.9	 -0.7   -1.2</p>
<p> Calendar-adjusted yr/yr		 5.1	 -2.1   -3.9</p>
<p>The INE gave the following breakdown (percentage change):</p>
<p>					     JAN 97   DEC  96 YR-TO-DATE</p>
<p> Energy					1.7	 -1.8    1.7</p>
<p> Non-energy minerals, chemicals     -3.6	  2.8   -3.6</p>
<p> Metals, precision tools		 4.4	  2.4    4.4</p>
<p> Other manufacturing		     6.6	  2.5    6.6</p>
<p> Consumer goods			    5.3	  2.3    5.3</p>
<p> Capital goods			     6.5	  3.0    6.5</p>
<p> Intermediary goods			0.3	  0.9    0.3</p>
</text>
